-- a λ that is a value (a closure): a new definition whose parameters are the λ's free variables
-- then its own leading binders, and the value the definition applied to the free variables alone
-- (a partial application, which encodes as a closure cell). λ-lifting: the definition applied to
-- the free variables is the λ, which the code's meaning computes identically
-- the lifting of a list, and of branches under their fields' binders (not taken for closures)
x-lift-l : (Code → LS → Code × LS) → Lst Code → LS → Lst Code × LS
x-lift-l f lnil st = (lnil , st)
x-lift-l f (lcons x xs) st = (let r1 = f x st in let r2 = x-lift-l f xs (snd r1) in (lcons (fst r1) (fst r2) , snd r2))
